 ## Overview
-This method describes the binary parsing and deserialization of the OpenVDB (VDB) file format to reconstruct the hierarchical sparse voxel grid in memory [S1, unofficial]. It converts the compact, compressed on-disk representation into a traversable in-memory tree structure suitable for rendering or simulation [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from generic VDB loading by its explicit handling of the specific binary layout of Node5 and Node4 hierarchies, including the complex logic for decompressing active masks and inactive values [S1, unofficial].
+This method describes the binary parsing of the OpenVDB file format to reconstruct the hierarchical sparse voxel grid structure in memory. It solves the problem of converting the compact, compressed on-disk representation into a traversable in-memory tree suitable for rendering or simulation. It is distinguished from generic VDB loading by its explicit handling of the specific binary layout of GridDescriptors, Metadata, and the compressed Node5/Node4/Node3 hierarchy, including the expansion of active masks and inactive value storage [S1, unofficial].
 
